1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,241
I told the sailors to throw me into the sea

2
00:00:02,261 --> 00:00:04,862
— and a great fish swallowed me whole, and

3
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:06,282
buried me alive in the dark.

4
00:00:07,422 --> 00:00:09,963
I ran from God because His mercy was too wide.

5
00:00:10,783 --> 00:00:12,824
He sent me to Nineveh, and I fled.

6
00:00:13,824 --> 00:00:15,925
I knew He is gracious, and would spare her.

7
00:00:17,065 --> 00:00:19,646
The storm came for my sake; the lot fell on

8
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:19,986
me.

9
00:00:20,726 --> 00:00:23,887
Then, centuries later, scribes demanded a sign

10
00:00:23,907 --> 00:00:28,089
— Jesus gave them only my name: For as Jonas

11
00:00:28,129 --> 00:00:30,329
was three days and three nights in the whale's

12
00:00:30,349 --> 00:00:33,831
belly; so shall the Son of man be three days

13
00:00:33,931 --> 00:00:36,932
and three nights in the heart of the earth.

14
00:00:37,592 --> 00:00:39,932
I went down guilty — the storm was mine.

15
00:00:40,613 --> 00:00:43,033
He went down innocent, bearing what was ours;

16
00:00:43,694 --> 00:00:44,514
He gave Himself.

17
00:00:45,114 --> 00:00:47,475
The grave no more held Him than the deep held

18
00:00:47,515 --> 00:00:47,815
me.

19
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:49,095
He rose.

20
00:00:49,956 --> 00:00:52,516
You who are sure you've fallen too far — that

21
00:00:52,576 --> 00:00:54,117
is how far His mercy reaches.

22
00:00:54,897 --> 00:00:57,298
The One who went down into your dark and rose

23
00:00:57,358 --> 00:00:58,838
again is Jesus.

24
00:00:59,699 --> 00:01:00,779
He can bring you up.
